{"availability":"available","full":"Flowdesktech/flowvault","name":"flowvault","description":"Privacy-first notepad: Argon2id + AES-256-GCM, hidden-volume plausible deniability (N notebooks per URL), optimistic concurrency, dead-man's switch, drand/tlock time-locked notes, and one-shot encrypted send. Next.js frontend, Firebase Functions, auditable Firestore rules. MIT.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":76,"forks":31,"created":"2026-04-20T04:39:17Z","updated":"2026-08-25T06:46:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://useflowvault.com","topics":["aes-gcm","argon2id","client-side-encryption","cryptpad-alternative","encrypted-notepad","end-to-end-encryption","firebase","firestore","hidden-volumes","nextjs","plausible-deniability","privacy-tools","privnote-alternative","protectedtext-alternative","self-hostable","standard-notes-alternative","tailwindcss","trusted-handover","typescript","zero-knowledge"],"demo":"https://useflowvault.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.365Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.365Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.365Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.365Z","stars":76,"forks":31}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The encrypted notepad where a decoy password is a feature, not a bug. Pick a URL, set a password, write. One Flowvault link can hold up to 64 independent notebooks behind 64 different passwords &mdash; each unlocks its own workspace, and the server sees one indistinguishable blob either way. Hand over a decoy if you&rsquo;re ever forced to; your real notebook stays invisible.","1 URL · up to 64 notebooks · 512 KiB total · Argon2id + AES-256-GCM · no account · open source end-to-end","Try it · 1min intro (video) · Blog · Security · Self-host · Donate"],"features":["Hidden-volume vaults — the headline feature. One URL, N notebooks, one blob. If someone coerces a password out of you at a border crossing, you hand over the decoy. Cryptographically indistinguishable from a…","Multi-notebook tabs — each password now unlocks a workspace, not just one page. Add tabs, rename them, reorder them, delete them. Everything lives inside the same encrypted slot, so the tab list, titles, and contents…","Time-locked notes — encrypt a message to a future date using the drand public randomness beacon and the tlock scheme (identity-based encryption over BLS12-381). The ciphertext is stored opaquely; the decryption key…","Encrypted Send — one-shot, self-destructing notes for sharing a password, an API key, a recovery phrase, or any snippet you'd rather not sit in chat history. AES-256-GCM encrypted in the browser; the 256-bit key travels…","Encrypted File Send — same threat model as Encrypted Send, but for actual files. Drop a file (up to 10 MiB), pick an expiry (max 7 days) and a download cap (default 1, max 10), and you get back two links: a download…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Flowdesktech/flowvault/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"fe08875745572ac39adac6ff7044c764be3cdd1ee76ab1e2a541c721587ed503","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.481Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:38.481Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The encrypted notepad where a decoy password is a feature, not a bug. Pick a URL, set a password, write. One Flowvault link can hold up to 64 independent notebooks behind 64 different passwords &mdash; each unlocks its own workspace, and the server sees one indistinguishable blob either way. Hand over a decoy if you&rsquo;re ever forced to; your real notebook stays invisible.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Flowdesktech/flowvault/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"> 1 URL · up to 64 notebooks · 512 KiB total · Argon2id + AES-256-GCM · no account · open source end-to-end","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Flowdesktech/flowvault/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"hos